# Client refactor safety backups (CLIENT_REFACTORING_PLAN.md, Phase 0.1).
#
# Backups such as _client-backup-<timestamp>/ are created beside Proxy Client/
# and are several MB each. Ignoring them keeps them out of a stray `git add .`
# and, more importantly, makes `git clean -fd` skip them: git clean only removes
# ignored files when -x is passed, and losing a backup to a cleanup is exactly
# the failure mode this plan exists to avoid.
_client-backup-*/

# Bot Workshop generated exports (BOT_TOOLING.md T1).
#
# These are derived entirely from Data/world and Data/cfg: a full-world export is ~500 MB and
# rebuilding it takes about five seconds, so it is a build artefact rather than content. The
# tool's *inputs* live in Data/cfg and are committed by hand; only its output is ignored.
Proxy Server/Data/workshop/

# The same export, written to the JDT output directories by a run whose working directory was
# jdt-bin rather than the project root. Identical content to the line above; ignored for the
# same reason, so a stray run cannot dirty the tree.
jdt-bin/workshop/
Proxy Server/jdt-bin/workshop/
